// Tessera stdlib: pieces shared by the F64 arc sine and arc cosine
//
// The double-double helpers (a sum with its rounding error, a double-double
// sum, a double-double product) and the two tables both functions read: the
// piecewise polynomial of asin(x)/x in x^2, and sin(j pi/64) as double-doubles
// for the accurate path's rotation. atan and atan2 use the double-double
// record and the fast two-sum too.
//
// Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binary64/asin/asin.c and src/binary64/acos/acos.c
// via RazorForge's B64Asin.rf and B64Acos.rf.
// Copyright (c) 2022-2026 Alexei Sibidanov <sibid@uvic.ca>
// MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module Standard::Core

